		(uuid "4bc7ef7e-4ba7-4408-8f73-f8e319b33143")
	)
	(text "# BATTERY SUBSYSTEM DESIGN NOTES (BATTERY BLOCK)\nProject: OpenMycoNet BLE_BRIDGE\nStatus: READY FOR MANUFACTURING (JLCPCB 4-Layer Stackup)\nDate: 2026-10-25\nRevision: 2.3\n\nSYSTEM OVERVIEW\nThe battery subsystem manages dynamic power-path routing, lithium battery charging, hardware power switching, state-of-charge fuel gauging, and\nedge ground probing. It utilizes a BQ24075 power-path manager (U4) to seamlessly power downstream regulators (VDD) from either USB input (VBUS) or\na single-cell LiPo/Li-ion battery (+BATT). A MAX17048 fuel gauge (U5) provides battery telemetry over I2C, while a dedicated slide switch (S1)\ncontrols physical battery isolation.\n\n1. BATTERY CHARGER, POWER-PATH & POWER SWITCH (U4 BQ24075RGT)\n• Core IC: U4 (BQ24075RGT standalone Li-ion power-path manager).\n• Hardware Power Switch (S1): Slide switch S1 connected to Pin 15 (SYSOFF). Toggling S1 switches SYSOFF between GND (normal battery operation \n  power ON) and +BATT (battery disconnect / system OFF).\n• Input Mode Configuration (EN1/EN2): Pin 5 (EN2) is pulled HIGH to VBUS through a 10 kΩ resistor (R12), and Pin 6 (EN1) is tied LOW to GND. Per\n  Table 1 of the BQ24075 datasheet, this EN2=1, EN1=0 state configures External Resistor Mode via Pin 12 (ILIM) and ensures stable VDD passthrough\n  during batteryless USB operation.\n• Input Current Limit: Resistor R13 (1.18 kΩ) on Pin 12 (ILIM) configures the programmable maximum input current draw from VBUS to 1.35 A.\n• Fast-Charge Current: Resistor R14 (1.13 kΩ) on Pin 16 (ISET) sets fast-charge current to 787 mA.\n• Input Decoupling: C10 (1 µF) ceramic capacitor connected between VBUS input and GND.\n• Battery Terminal Connection: BAT pin (Pin 2) connects to the single-cell battery rail +BATT, decoupled by C12 (4.7 µF). Connected to 3-pin\n  battery connector J2 (BATT_CONN).\n• System Power Rail (VDD): OUT pin (Pin 10) provides the main system output rail VDD, decoupled by C11 (4.7 µF) and monitored by test point TP7.\n• Charge Enable: Pin 4 (~CE) pulled LOW to GND to enable automatic charging when VBUS is present.\n• Safety Timer: Pin 14 (TMR) tied to GND through R11 (46.4 kΩ) to set safety timer limits.\n• Thermal Protection: Pin 1 (TS) tied to 10 kΩ NTC thermistor TH1 on PCB as well as Pin 2 (NTC) of 3-pin J2 header to suspend charging during\n  over/under-temperature conditions. TH1 is designated DNP when using external pack NTC to prevent parallel resistance errors.\n• Status Monitors: ~PGOOD (Pin 7) pulled up to +3.3V via R15 (10 kΩ). ~CHG (Pin 9) pulled up to +3.3V via R16 (10 kΩ).\n• Static Power LEDs: Static PCB power/alert LEDs removed to eliminate continuous parasitic drain during deep sleep.\n\n2. FUEL GAUGE SETUP (U5 MAX17048G+T10)\n• Core IC: U5 (MAX17048G+T10 ModelGauge I2C fuel gauge).\n• Sensing & Power: CELL (Pin 2) and VDD (Pin 3) tied directly to the +BATT rail, decoupled by C13 (100 nF).\n• Grounding: GND (Pin 4), CTG (Pin 1), and Exposed Pad EP (Pin 9) connected directly to system GND.\n• I2C Telemetry: SCL (Pin 7) and SDA (Pin 8) routed to the shared I2C bus (I2C_BUS.SCL, I2C_BUS.SDA).\n• Interrupt Output: ALERT (Pin 5) drives active-LOW BATT_ALERT signal directly to MCU GPIO for low-power wake-up triggers.\n• Quick-Start Pin: QSTRT (Pin 6) tied to GND.\n\n3. PCB EDGE GROUNDING & TEST POINT ARRAY\n• Perimeter Ground Test Points: TP1, TP2, TP3, and TP4 placed at perimeter/corners for ground clips and chassis grounding checks.\n• System Supply Test Points: TP5 (+3.3V digital rail), TP6 (+3.3VA clean analog rail), and TP7 (VDD regulated supply output).\n\n4. INTERFACE MATRIX\n• VBUS: +5V power input supplied from the USB-C interface.\n• VDD: Regulated system power output driving downstream buck-boost converters (+3.3V / +3.3VA).\n• +BATT: Unregulated single-cell LiPo/Li-ion battery rail (3.0 V to 4.2 V nominal).\n• S1 (SWITCH): Hardware system power switch (toggles SYSOFF).\n• J2 (BATT_CONN): 3-pin header (+BATT, NTC, GND) for external battery pack interfacing.\n• TP5, TP6, TP7: System voltage test points (+3.3V, +3.3VA, VDD).\n• TP1-TP4: PCB perimeter Ground (GND) test points."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
